 += the packets transferred by its contacting T cells."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["Overdamped persistent-random-walk migration (velocity re-randomized each tick at the cell's speed); neighbors are within 1 um of the cells' membranes; a T cell polarizes to its single nearest tumor, a tumor collects all its T-cell neighbors."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}, "_outputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}}, "field": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:DiffusionField", "config": {"bounds_x": 200.0, "bounds_y": 200.0, "n_bins_x": 20, "n_bins_y": 20, "depth": 15.0, "molecules": ["IFNg"]}, "interval": 60.0, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"], "fields": ["fields"]}, "outputs": {"cells": ["cells"], "fields": ["fields"]}, "doc": "Soluble-field manager (tumor-tcell Fields + LocalField consolidated): deposits each cell's secreted amounts into its field bin, diffuses and decays the 2D IFNg / tumor-debris concentration grids (ng/mL), and samples each cell's local concentration back onto it.", "_contract": {"summary": "Soluble-field manager (tumor-tcell Fields + LocalField consolidated): deposits each cell's exchange counts into its field bin, diffuses + decays the 2D concentration fields, and samples each cell's local concentration back onto it.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); reads each cell's location (um) and exchange amounts (molecule counts).", "fields": "2D concentration grids per molecule (ng/mL) on an n_bins grid over bounds (um)."}, "outputs": {"cells": "Per cell: sampled local concentrations (local, ng/mL) and exchange reset; cells flagged dead are removed (_remove).", "fields": "Field deltas (ng/mL) after deposit + diffuse + decay."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["IFNg: D = 1.25e-3 cm^2/day, 4.5 h e-fold decay. tumor_debris: D = 0.0864 cm^2/day, no decay. Counts <-> concentration via Avogadro / molecular weight (IFNg 17000, debris 29000 g/mol) / bin volume (depth um)."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]", "fields": {"_type": "map", "_value": {"_type": "array", "_shape": [20, 20], "_data": "float"}}}, "_outputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]", "fields": {"_type": "map", "_value": {"_type": "array", "_shape": [20, 20], "_data": "float"}}}}, "tumor_behavior": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:TumorCellProcess", "config": {}, "interval": 60.0, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"]}, "outputs": {"cells": ["cells"]}, "doc": "Tumor cell behavior: proliferation, IFNg-driven PDL1n -> PDL1p phenotype conversion, and death by apoptosis or accumulated cytotoxic packets (releasing tumor debris). Ported from tumor_tcell/processes/tumor.py.", "_contract": {"summary": "Tumor cell behavior \u2014 proliferative PDL1n <-> arrested PDL1p. Internalizing enough IFNg (>= 15000 counts) flips PDL1n -> PDL1p (MHCI/PDL1-high, G0-arrested); dies by apoptosis or when received cytotoxic packets exceed threshold, releasing tumor_debris.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); per tumor cell reads cell_state, internal_IFNg (counts), receive_cytotoxic (packets), and sampled local IFNg concentration (ng/mL)."}, "outputs": {"cells": "Per tumor cell: PDL1n -> PDL1p switch; present_PDL1/present_MHCI equilibria (5e4) when PDL1p; IFNg internalization (internal_IFNg + / field exchange -); death (+ 1.4e15 tumor_debris); PDL1n division into two daughters (_add/_remove)."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["Only PDL1n tumors divide (PDL1p are arrested); death releases 1.4e15 debris molecules; diameter 15 um, mass 8 ng. Parameters transcribed from tumor-tcell / Hickey, Agmon et al., Cell Systems 2024."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}, "_outputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}}, "tcell_behavior": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:TCellProcess", "config": {}, "interval": 60.0, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"]}, "outputs": {"cells": ["cells"]}, "doc": "T cell behavior: on contact with a tumor it secretes IFNg and delivers cytotoxic packets; unengaged it migrates; sustained engagement drives PD1n -> PD1p exhaustion (reduced secretion). Ported from tumor_tcell/processes/t_cell.py.", "_contract": {"summary": "CD8+ T cell behavior \u2014 active PD1- <-> exhausted PD1+. In contact with an MHCI+ tumor it secretes IFNg (which converts tumors) and cytotoxic packets (which kill); TCR down-regulates after ~6 h of activation then a refractory period; repeated cycles or division count drive PD1- -> PD1+ exhaustion.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); per T cell reads cell_state, accept_MHCI / accept_PDL1 (from the contacted tumor), present_TCR, TCR + velocity timers (s), refractory / divide counts, and cytotoxic stockpile."}, "outputs": {"cells": "Per T cell: IFNg secretion (field exchange, counts) and transfer_cytotoxic (packets) in contact; TCR up/down-regulation; PD1- -> PD1+ exhaustion; migration speed (um/s, with dwell logic); division into two daughters (_add/_remove)."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["PD1- secretes ~10x more IFNg/cytotoxic than PD1+; production is 4-fold reduced vs an MHCI-low tumor; migration 10 (PD1-) / 5 (PD1+) um/min; diameter 7.5 um, mass 2 ng. Parameters from tumor-tcell."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}, "_outputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]"}}, "viz_populations": {"_type": "step", "address": "local:PopulationTimeseries", "config": {"title": "Cell populations over time"}, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"], "time": ["global_time"]}, "outputs": {"html": ["viz", "populations_html"]}, "doc": "Total and per-phenotype cell counts over time (tumor PDL1n/PDL1p, T cell PD1n/PD1p, dendritic) as an interactive Plotly line chart.", "_contract": {"summary": "Total + per-phenotype cell counts over time, rendered as an interactive Plotly line chart.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); counted by cell_type and cell_state each tick.", "time": "Simulation time (s); the x-axis (converted to hours)."}, "outputs": {"html": "Rendered Plotly HTML (line per count series: tumor total/PDL1n/PDL1p, T cell total/PD1n/PD1p, and dendritic when present)."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["Accumulates one count snapshot per tick; flat-zero series are dropped from the legend."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]", "time": "float"}, "_outputs": {"html": "string"}}, "viz_phenotypes": {"_type": "step", "address": "local:PhenotypeFractions", "config": {"title": "Phenotype conversion over time"}, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"], "time": ["global_time"]}, "outputs": {"html": ["viz", "phenotypes_html"]}, "doc": "PDL1+ tumor fraction and PD1+ T-cell fraction over time (Plotly) \u2014 the paper's headline readout, tracking the rate of IFNg-driven phenotype conversion rather than raw kill count.", "_contract": {"summary": "PDL1+ tumor fraction and PD1+ T-cell fraction over time \u2014 the paper's IFNg-driven conversion readout.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); the PDL1p tumor fraction and PD1p T-cell fraction are computed each tick.", "time": "Simulation time (s); the x-axis (converted to hours)."}, "outputs": {"html": "Rendered Plotly HTML (fraction in 0-1 vs time, one line per fraction)."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["Fractions are 0 when the denominator population (tumors / T cells) is empty."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]", "time": "float"}, "_outputs": {"html": "string"}}, "viz_spatial": {"_type": "step", "address": "local:SpatialLayout", "config": {"title": "Spatial layout over the IFNg field", "bounds_x": 200.0, "bounds_y": 200.0, "field": "IFNg"}, "inputs": {"cells": ["cells"], "fields": ["fields"], "time": ["global_time"]}, "outputs": {"html": ["viz", "spatial_html"]}, "doc": "Animated GIF of cells (true circles in \u00b5m) over the IFNg field, colored by type/state \u2014 the interactive analogue of the paper's videos.", "_contract": {"summary": "Animated GIF of cells over the IFNg field \u2014 true circles in um data-coordinates, colored by type/state; the interactive analogue of the paper's videos.", "description": "", "inputs": {"cells": "All cells (map[tumor_tcell_agent]); reads location (um), radius (um), cell_type, cell_state per tick.", "fields": "2D concentration grids per molecule (ng/mL); the IFNg grid is drawn as the background heatmap.", "time": "Simulation time (s); frame timestamps."}, "outputs": {"html": "A standalone HTML page embedding an autoplaying, looping GIF (matplotlib)."}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": ["Buffers a compact frame per tick; the GIF is rendered once at end-of-run (max_frames subsampling for a smooth, lightweight animation)."], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"cells": "map[tumor_tcell_agent]", "fields": {"_type": "map", "_value": {"_type": "array", "_data": "float"}}, "time": "float"}, "_outputs": {"html": "string"}}}, "schema": {}, "overrides": {}, "requires": {}, "tags": [], "visualizations": [], "analyses": [], "emitters": [], "kind": "generator", "module": "viva_tumor_tcell.composites.microenvironment", "default_n_steps": 500, "svg": null, "wiring_status": "ready", "run_kind": "temporal", "notice": null}